			<h1>Search Engines Without AI</h1>
			<p class="intro">A comparison of search engines that don't force AI summaries on you.</p>

			<nav class="toc">
				<h2>Contents</h2>
				<ol>
					<li><a href="#comparison">Quick Comparison</a></li>
					<li><a href="#google">Google (with AI disabled)</a></li>
					<li><a href="#duckduckgo">DuckDuckGo</a></li>
					<li><a href="#brave">Brave Search</a></li>
					<li><a href="#startpage">Startpage</a></li>
					<li><a href="#qwant">Qwant</a></li>
					<li><a href="#mojeek">Mojeek</a></li>
					<li><a href="#presearch">Presearch</a></li>
					<li><a href="#others">Other Options</a></li>
					<li><a href="#recommendation">Our Recommendation</a></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>

			<section id="comparison">
				<h2>Quick Comparison</h2>
				<div class="table-wrapper">
					<table>
						<thead>
							<tr>
								<th>Engine</th>
								<th>AI Default</th>
								<th>Can Disable AI</th>
								<th>Index</th>
								<th>Privacy</th>
							</tr>
						</thead>
						<tbody>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Google</strong></td>
								<td class="status-bad">On</td>
								<td class="status-good">Yes (udm=14)</td>
								<td>Own</td>
								<td>Low</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>DuckDuckGo</strong></td>
								<td class="status-warn">Optional</td>
								<td class="status-good">Yes</td>
								<td>Bing</td>
								<td>High</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Brave</strong></td>
								<td class="status-warn">Optional</td>
								<td class="status-good">Yes</td>
								<td>Own</td>
								<td>High</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Startpage</strong></td>
								<td class="status-good">None</td>
								<td>N/A</td>
								<td>Google</td>
								<td>High</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Qwant</strong></td>
								<td class="status-good">None</td>
								<td>N/A</td>
								<td>Own + Bing</td>
								<td>High</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Mojeek</strong></td>
								<td class="status-good">None</td>
								<td>N/A</td>
								<td>Own</td>
								<td>High</td>
							</tr>
							<tr>
								<td><strong>Presearch</strong></td>
								<td class="status-good">None</td>
								<td>N/A</td>
								<td>Multiple</td>
								<td>High</td>
							</tr>
						</tbody>
					</table>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="google">
				<h2>Google (with AI Disabled)</h2>
				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag">Best Results</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>Google still has the best search index, but AI Overview can be annoying. The good news: you can disable it.</p>

					<h3>How to Disable AI</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>udm=14</strong> - Add to URL for "Web" filter (most reliable)</li>
						<li><strong>-ai suffix</strong> - Add "-ai" to your query (less reliable)</li>
						<li><strong>Unslop Search</strong> - Use our tool to add it automatically</li>
					</ul>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Best search quality</li>
								<li>Largest index</li>
								<li>AI is fully removable</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Privacy concerns</li>
								<li>Requires workaround for AI</li>
								<li>Tracking-heavy</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<a href="/guides/disable-ai-overview-google" class="learn-more">Learn how to disable Google AI &rarr;</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="duckduckgo">
				<h2>DuckDuckGo</h2>
				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag">Privacy Focused</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>Privacy-focused search engine that uses Bing's index. Has AI features but they're optional and can be disabled.</p>

					<h3>How to Disable AI</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>noai.duckduckgo.com</strong> - Official AI-free subdomain (recommended)</li>
						<li><strong>URL params</strong> - Add <code>kbg=-1&kbe=-1&kbd=-1</code> to disable AI features</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>AI Features (All Optional)</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Duck.ai</strong> - AI chat (disabled on noai subdomain)</li>
						<li><strong>AI Assist / Search Assist</strong> - AI answers (disabled on noai subdomain)</li>
						<li><strong>AI Images</strong> - Filtered out on noai subdomain</li>
					</ul>

					<h3>Other AI-Free Versions</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><code>noai.duckduckgo.com</code> - Official AI-free version (best option)</li>
						<li><code>html.duckduckgo.com</code> - HTML-only, no JavaScript</li>
						<li><code>lite.duckduckgo.com</code> - Lightweight text-only version</li>
					</ul>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Strong privacy</li>
								<li>No tracking</li>
								<li>Good bangs (!g, !w, etc.)</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Uses Bing's index</li>
								<li>Results less comprehensive</li>
								<li>AI settings can reset</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="brave">
				<h2>Brave Search</h2>
				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag">Independent Index</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>Built by the Brave browser team with their own search index. AI is opt-in, not default.</p>

					<h3>AI Features</h3>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Answer with AI</strong> - Only appears when you click the button</li>
						<li><strong>Leo AI</strong> - In Brave browser only (can be disabled in settings)</li>
						<li>Disable with <code>summary=0</code> parameter</li>
					</ul>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Own search index</li>
								<li>AI is opt-in</li>
								<li>No tracking</li>
								<li>Good quality</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Smaller index than Google</li>
								<li>Some queries less comprehensive</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="startpage">
				<h2>Startpage</h2>
				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag green">No AI</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>A privacy proxy for Google search. Get Google results without being tracked by Google.</p>

					<h3>AI Features</h3>
					<p><strong>None.</strong> Startpage doesn't add any AI features to results.</p>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Google-quality results</li>
								<li>Complete privacy</li>
								<li>No AI by default</li>
								<li>Anonymous View feature</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Can be slower</li>
								<li>Sometimes rate-limited</li>
								<li>No personalization</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<a href="/guides/startpage-search-engine" class="learn-more">Learn more about Startpage &rarr;</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="qwant">
				<h2>Qwant</h2>
				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag green">No AI</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>European privacy-focused search engine based in France. Uses their own index supplemented by Bing.</p>

					<h3>AI Features</h3>
					<p><strong>None by default.</strong> "AI Flash Answer" only appears if you specifically request it.</p>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>EU-based (GDPR compliant)</li>
								<li>No tracking</li>
								<li>No AI by default</li>
								<li>Kids version (Qwant Junior)</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Smaller index</li>
								<li>Better for EU content</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<a href="/guides/qwant-search-engine" class="learn-more">Learn more about Qwant &rarr;</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="mojeek">
				<h2>Mojeek</h2>
				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag green">No AI</span>
							<span class="engine-tag">Own Index</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>UK-based search engine with its own independently crawled index. Not based on Google or Bing.</p>

					<h3>AI Features</h3>
					<p><strong>None.</strong> Has an optional "Summarize" feature but it's manual and opt-in.</p>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Truly independent index</li>
								<li>No tracking</li>
								<li>Transparent ranking</li>
								<li>No AI forced</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Smaller index</li>
								<li>Less comprehensive results</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<a href="/guides/mojeek-search-engine" class="learn-more">Learn more about Mojeek &rarr;</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="presearch">
				<h2>Presearch</h2>
				<div class="engine-card">
					<div class="engine-header">
						<div class="engine-info">
							<span class="engine-tag green">No AI</span>
							<span class="engine-tag">Decentralized</span>
						</div>
					</div>
					<p>Decentralized search engine that aggregates results from multiple sources. Community-driven with crypto rewards.</p>

					<h3>AI Features</h3>
					<p><strong>None.</strong> Focus is on decentralization and user privacy, not AI.</p>

					<div class="pros-cons">
						<div class="pros">
							<h4>Pros</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Decentralized</li>
								<li>Multiple sources</li>
								<li>No AI</li>
								<li>Earn PRE tokens</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
						<div class="cons">
							<h4>Cons</h4>
							<ul>
								<li>Results vary</li>
								<li>Less refined</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</div>

					<a href="/guides/presearch-search-engine" class="learn-more">Learn more about Presearch &rarr;</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section id="others">
				<h2>Other Options</h2>

				<div class="other-engines">
					<div class="other-engine">
						<h3>SearXNG</h3>
						<p>Open-source metasearch engine. No AI, self-hostable, aggregates results from multiple engines.</p>
						<a href="https://searx.space" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Find public instances</a>
					</div>

					<div class="other-engine">
						<h3>MetaGer</h3>
						<p>German non-profit metasearch. No AI, supports Tor, privacy-focused.</p>
						<a href="https://metager.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">metager.org</a>
					</div>

					<div class="other-engine">
						<h3>Ecosia</h3>
						<p>Plants trees with ad revenue. Has optional AI Overview that can be disabled in settings.</p>
						<a href="https://ecosia.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ecosia.org</a>
					</div>
				</div>

				<h3>Engines to Avoid (If You Want No AI)</h3>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Bing</strong> - Copilot is heavily integrated, toggle to disable is unreliable</li>
					<li><strong>Yahoo</strong> - No way to disable AI</li>
					<li><strong>Perplexity</strong> - AI is the core product</li>
					<li><strong>ChatGPT Search</strong> - AI is the core product</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section id="recommendation">
				<h2>Our Recommendation</h2>
				<div class="recommendation-card">
					<h3>Use Unslop Search</h3>
					<p>Get the best of all worlds:</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Google quality</strong> with AI disabled via udm=14</li>
						<li><strong>Switch easily</strong> between Google, DuckDuckGo, Brave, and others</li>
						<li><strong>Remember your choice</strong> - preferences are saved locally</li>
						<li><strong>Set as default</strong> - use it from your browser's address bar</li>
					</ul>
					<p>All search engines in Unslop Search have their AI features disabled automatically.</p>
					<a href="/" class="cta-button">Try Unslop Search</a>
				</div>
			</section>

			<div class="next-steps">
				<h2>Next Steps</h2>
				<div class="next-links">
					<a href="/guides/disable-ai-overview-google">
						<span>Guide</span>
						<strong>Disable Google AI</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/what-is-udm14">
						<span>Technical</span>
						<strong>What is udm=14?</strong>
					</a>
					<a href="/guides/browser-extension">
						<span>Install</span>
						<strong>Browser Extension</strong>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</body>
</html>

